tml?id=THdwEAAAQBAJ)\nciteturn364search3 [wordlim: 200] Published: 3.7 years ago; Crawled: last month; \n### About the author (2023)\n\nBruce Schneier is a renowned security technologist who has written over one dozen books, including the New York Times bestseller Data and Goliath and Click Here to Kill Everybody. He teaches at the Harvard Kennedy School and lives in Cambridge, Massachusetts.\n\n### Bibliographic information\n\nTitle  | A Hacker's Mind: How the Powerful Bend Society's Rules, and How to Bend them Back\nAuthor  | Bruce Schneier\nPublisher  | W. W. Norton & Company, 2023\nISBN  | 039386667X, 9780393866674\nLength  | 304 pages\nSubjects  | Computers › Security › General\nComputers / Security / General\nComputers / Social Aspects\nPolitical Science / Security (National & International)\nSocial Science / Technology Studies\n   |  \nExport Citation  | BiBTeX EndNote RefMan--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nA brief history of time travel | Nature Physics (https://www.nature.com/articles/nphys3910)\nciteturn364search4 [wordlim: 200] Published: 10.1 years ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; \n\n  * Books & Arts\n  * Published: 04 October 2016\n\nConversation\n\n# A brief history of time travel\n\n  * Dave Goldberg ^{1} \n\nNature Physics volume 12, page 892 (2016)\n\n## Time Travel: A History\n\n  * James Gleick\n\nis available through Pantheon Books.\n\nIn his brisk and entertaining new book, Time Travel: A History, James Gleick serves as an enthusiastic guide through the fourth dimension as seen in literature and popular culture. I spoke with Gleick to discuss his book, the interface between science and science fiction and what makes genuinely compelling time travel.\n\n## Author information\n\n### Authors and Affiliations\n\n  1. Dave Goldberg is in the Department of Physics, Drexel University, Philadelphia, Pennsylvania 19104, USA,\n\nDave Goldberg \n\n### Corresponding author\n\nCorrespondence to Dave Goldberg  